course: dictionary
lesson: 12917
title: Estranged: no longer close
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Estranged is a word you will meet in stories and news about families. It means no longer close to someone, usually a family member, or a husband or wife, because you have stopped speaking or living together. «Mia had not spoken to her estranged father for five years.» The word tells you that they were once close, but that bond has been broken.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «After the big argument, the two brothers became estranged.» The words after the argument show what caused the break. Estranged often comes after a quarrel, so the reader knows the split was real and not just a long gap.
explain: The word can also be used in a more formal way, to mean feeling cut off from something you once belonged to. «Years after she moved away, Amira felt estranged from the village where she grew up.» She still knows the village, but it no longer feels like hers. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
fact: Estranged means no longer close to someone.
fact: It is usually used for a family member, or a husband or wife.
fact: «An estranged wife» is a wife who has stopped speaking to her husband or living with him.
fact: Estranged often describes a break that came after a quarrel.
fact: A good check is to swap in a word like "close" and see if the sentence makes sense in the opposite way.
exercise: «His estranged father never came to his birthday party.» What does estranged mean here? | Still very close and in touch | Happy and full of fun | *No longer close, after they stopped speaking | Lost in a big city
exercise: «After the quarrel, the sisters became estranged for years.» What caused the break between them? | *A quarrel | A birthday party | A long summer holiday | A new school
exercise: «She felt estranged from her old school friends after moving away.» What does estranged suggest? | Feeling extremely excited | Singing loudly in class | Being on holiday abroad | *Feeling apart from people she once belonged with
test: «The estranged couple lived in different towns and rarely spoke.» What does estranged mean? | Busy with work | Angry at a football match | Married and very happy | *No longer close, and not living or speaking together
test: Which situation is most likely to leave people estranged? | A walk in the park together | Learning to swim | A shared birthday cake | *A long quarrel that was never mended
exam: «Mum's estranged brother visited after ten years, and they hugged on the doorstep.» What does estranged tell you about Mum and her brother? | They lived next door and saw each other every day | *They had lost touch and were no longer close | They had just met for the first time | They were famous singers on tour
